(text "ASSEMBLY, BRING-UP AND MOUNTING NOTES" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 14.000 17.000 0) (effects (font (size 3.0 3.0) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "3fdd0f25-aa7b-4962-b66e-4c749a598877"))
(text "Boards ordered as JLCPCB turnkey (SMT + THT terminals); Teensy and its headers are hand-fitted." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 14.000 21.500 0) (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e12ad1a9-41d9-4517-b939-d81cb66fafad"))
(polyline (pts (xy 14.000 23.000) (xy 418.000 23.000)) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "70448903-fc13-484d-9930-26df04edaef7"))
(text "1. TEENSY 4.1 (U1) - HAND SOLDER" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 14.000 28.000 0) (effects (font (size 2.4 2.4) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "77293e44-c5c0-419e-ba65-11932dba8e4f"))
(text "Solder two 1x24 female headers (HC-PM254-8.5H-1x24PZ, C41376163) into the U1 footprint, then plug the Teensy in." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 32.500 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "efca8eaf-2eb4-42d8-b860-fd3ed6a9a618"))
(text "CUT the VIN-VUSB pad on the underside of the Teensy (near the USB connector) with a knife: the board feeds Teensy VIN from the 5 V buck through D9." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 36.700 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6771de93-9004-4e6d-aa8c-2acb0c5b7d2c"))
(text "Do not connect USB and an external 5 V to VIN without this cut. USB programming then works with the board powered or unpowered (D9 isolates)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 40.900 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f341dcdf-b523-4e42-8ada-e76373dadafc"))
(text "No battery is fitted (VBAT unconnected). Programming button/ON-OFF pads are not wired." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 45.100 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f073df52-b26d-44c9-9aeb-b33914c5dc6a"))
(text "2. HX711 RATE JUMPERS (SJ1-SJ3)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 14.000 52.300 0) (effects (font (size 2.4 2.4) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0af09279-91cc-4361-bd86-e4c0945d183e"))
(text "Each HX711 RATE pin goes to the centre pad of a 3-way solder jumper: default bridge 1-2 = +3V3 = 80 SPS." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 56.800 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "884ff2aa-e43f-4867-be22-5d18b8d46f9d"))
(text "To run 10 SPS: cut the 1-2 bridge with a knife and bridge 2-3 (GND). RATE high is referenced to DVDD = 3.3 V." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 61.000 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0930f71e-a2d2-417c-9a82-6efa2eccb091"))
(text "Firmware: read all three HX711 DOUT lines together on the shared SCK (pins 3, 0, 1 and clock pin 2)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 65.200 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d641719b-5ee7-4eaa-8cf8-3124850bee24"))
(text "3. E-STOP WIRING (J32) AND FIRST POWER-UP" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 14.000 72.400 0) (effects (font (size 2.4 2.4) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0153112e-8e90-4bb6-9421-ada7cc5cc7ad"))
(text "Wire the E-stop NC contact block(s) to J32: contact A pins 1-2, contact B pins 3-4 (see sheet 4). Fit E-stop (or a jumper across pins 1-2) BEFORE applying 12 V or the valves will stay off." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 76.900 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "799e82d8-1f76-47e1-8fa4-55eeac308580"))
(text "Power up with no valves attached: measure +5 V (C1) and +3V3, check Teensy powers and ESTOP_IN reads HIGH with E-stop closed." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 81.100 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "07cc6fc9-cc84-4a93-9ff2-56150d02f88e"))
(text "Press E-stop: +12V_VALVE must drop to 0 V while +5 V / +3V3 / Teensy stay on; ESTOP_IN reads LOW. Release (reset) and valves re-arm automatically: add a firmware latch." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 85.300 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a9bd4a31-abb1-48e1-8566-2a276e90cec8"))
(text "With a bench supply set to 12 V / 1 A first, then 15 A supply with valves on." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 89.500 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0a6e58eb-0a72-4e12-a843-bacc2dddf0ed"))
(text "4. 12 V INPUT" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 14.000 96.700 0) (effects (font (size 2.4 2.4) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "44e0c435-e3c3-4742-9a43-f40f2bbad51c"))
(text "Use >= 14 AWG for the supply lead. Fuse F1 (20 A fast) is not resettable: fuse failure means a fault, find it before replacing." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 101.200 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "276e479c-b2a7-4446-a7bb-b2d063da6d63"))
(text "A reversed supply is blocked by Q8 (nothing downstream is powered, F1 does not blow)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 105.400 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8815f9bf-4851-4a56-a070-0cb4a606a4c1"))
(text "Supply must be 12 V DC +/- 10% at >= 15 A (all 7 valves ON) or sequence the valves in firmware." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 109.600 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "43bd6151-3155-4b08-b3b5-65282bc0a013"))
(text "5. MOUNTING (L-BRACKET)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 14.000 116.800 0) (effects (font (size 2.4 2.4) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d06b8634-cd43-4e83-a4f5-44d564036fb4"))
(text "Four M3 holes (3.2 mm NPTH) 4.0 mm from each board edge: hole centres 134.5 mm x 130.0 mm apart (sheet 8)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 121.300 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "05c450cf-a459-4d38-8bc4-17c4763d50fb"))
(text "Use M3 standoffs (nylon or metal) 8-10 mm tall under the bracket: the board must not touch the bracket (copper keepout 7 mm diameter around each hole)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 125.500 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "3da8b7b7-28a5-4173-acde-e78af1641d33"))
(text "Panel wiring (E-stop, switches on DI_1..DI_8, displays J29-J31) enters from the front edge where terminals face out." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 129.700 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "cbae0a71-190d-46ab-9af3-dc9acf24dc02"))
